## Prerequisites

Install these tools before working on NAHPU:

- [Git](https://git-scm.com/downloads)
- [Dart SDK](https://dart.dev/get-dart)
- [Flutter SDK](https://flutter.dev/docs/get-started/install)
- [Rust toolchain](https://rustup.rs/)
- [flutter_rust_bridge](https://cjycode.com/flutter_rust_bridge/)
- [GitHub CLI](https://cli.github.com/) *(optional)*

## Local setup

{% steps %}

1. Install Flutter using the official guide for your operating system.

   Run `flutter doctor` and resolve the reported issues before continuing.

   ```bash
   flutter doctor
   ```

2. Install Rust.

   {% tabs %}
   {% tabitem label="macOS / Linux" %}
   ```bash
   curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -sSf https://sh.rustup.rs | sh
   rustc --version
   ```
   {% /tabitem %}
   {% tabitem label="Windows" %}
   Download and run `rustup-init.exe` from [rustup.rs](https://rustup.rs/), then
   verify the installation.

   ```powershell
   rustc --version
   ```
   {% /tabitem %}
   {% /tabs %}

3. Install Flutter Rust Bridge codegen.

   ```bash
   cargo install flutter_rust_bridge_codegen
   ```

4. Make sure Cargo binaries are on your `PATH`.

   {% tabs %}
   {% tabitem label="macOS / Linux" %}
   ```bash
   export PATH="$HOME/.cargo/bin:$PATH"
   ```

   Add that line to your shell config, such as `~/.zshrc` or `~/.bashrc`.
   {% /tabitem %}
   {% tabitem label="Windows" %}
   Add `%USERPROFILE%\.cargo\bin` to your system `PATH` in Environment
   Variables.
   {% /tabitem %}
   {% /tabs %}

5. Clone NAHPU and get dependencies.

   ```bash
   git clone https://github.com/nahpu/nahpu.git
   cd nahpu
   flutter pub get
   ```

6. Run the app.

   ```bash
   flutter run
   ```

   {% aside type="caution" title="Attention Mac Users" %}

   If you are running on macOS, we recommend using the iOS simulator. This way it will avoid signing issues and having to modify the Xcode project. If you are modifying the Xcode project, please do not commit the changes to the respository.

   {% /aside %}

{% /steps %}

## Useful commands

```bash
# Analyze Dart code
flutter analyze

# Run Dart tests
flutter test

# Generate Drift, Riverpod, and other Dart generated code
dart run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs

# Generate Flutter Rust Bridge bindings
flutter_rust_bridge_codegen generate

# Run cargo check in rust/
python scripts.py frb --check

# Cleaning up build artifacts. Do this regularly to save disk space.
flutter clean

# For cleaning up Rust build artifacts, run this in the rust/ directory.
cd rust/
cargo clean
```
